      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why the preference for explicit unlock - are you worried about the performance of defer? In this case I agree that the impact is negligable because this isn\u0027t a hot code path.\n\nBut it does seem to be idomatic and widely accepted to use defer to release locks. There is a readability/maintainability advantage where you don\u0027t have to release the lock explicitly wherever you return and if anything panics during function execution then the lock is still released. I would usually prioritize these advantages over performance unless performance becomes and issue and needs to be optimized.",
